# Episode scripts

Follow **Episode script authoring** and the JSON schema in `PLAN.md`. Do not invent a different schema.

Prompting follows LTX-2.3 docs (cinematographer shot list, not poetry): [prompt adherence](https://ltx.io/blog/how-to-improve-ltx-2-3-prompt-adherence), [dialogue/acting](https://ltx.io/blog/directing-dialogue-and-acting), [character consistency](https://ltx.io/blog/how-to-maintain-character-consistency-in-ai-video), [I2V](https://ltx.io/blog/ltx-2-image-to-video-text-to-video-workflow), [2.3 template](https://ltx23.github.io/ltx-2-3-prompt-template/). `enhance_prompt` is off; write the real prompt.

- Read `characters/*.json` and `locations/*.json` first. Use only those `id`s and `views` keys.
- Every scene has `characterIds`, `locationId`, and `locationView`. Same room = same `locationId`. Same camera on that wall = same `locationView`.
- **Anchoring:** do not restate hair/wardrobe/set. The pipeline prepends the character `promptBlock` and location `preserve`. Scene text is blocking + motion only.
- **Screen-space:** `left` / `right` are the audience’s frame, not the character’s left/right. Write `screen-left`, `screen-right`, `lower-right of the gold frame`. Use `her right hand` only for which hand.
- **Beats:** one main action per 2–3 seconds of `durationSeconds` (LTX). Distilled clips: one physical action + at most two spoken phrases. Do not stack five actions in one prompt.
- **Chronology:** subject + main action first, then gesture, then speech beats, then camera, then audio last.

## `imagePrompt` (Qwen start still = LTX frame 0)

Blocking the camera will see. No motion, no speech, no camera size (that is `locationView`).

- Eyeline: what she looks at. If she is not addressing the lens, write **not looking at camera**.
- Body angle, which hand, where the prop sits, lips slightly parted if she speaks this clip.
- Hands must reach what they touch. Place props in screen-space (`sealed envelope in the gap at the lower-right of the frame`, not “on her chest”).
- Do not contradict the chosen view (no “hands on the portrait” against an establishing wide).

## `videoPrompt` (LTX I2V)

Describe **what happens next**, not the still (I2V already has the picture). Literal, chronological, under ~200 words.

- Interleave speech: short phrase, one acting cue, next phrase. Cues: eyeline, pause, voice quality, or a physical beat — **one cue per beat**. Do not dump a full quoted sentence with no pause.
- Always name camera: `Camera static` or `Camera slow push-in`. Slow moves that underline a beat; no wide pans during dialogue.
- Audio last: acoustic space + matching foley, **no music**. Off-screen voices steal the line.
- Do not fight the start frame (no new wardrobe, room, or prop). Gaze between phrases is fine; do not replace the spoken line with “looks past the camera.”

One speaker. English only. No crowds, fights, morphs, 360s, on-screen text, mid-clip identity/set changes. Size `durationSeconds` to the beats. Valid episode JSON only unless the human asked for a plan first.
